me

21
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:14,820
me

22
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:31,740
Lottery-ticket bum dreaming
of striking it rich!

23
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:39,920
Thank you for your business!

24
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:41,820
Please come again.

25
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:47,220
You make me blow twenty thousand yen
in five hours on my precious day off,

26
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:50,180
and what's this about one cup noodle?

27
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:52,360
And it's before payday!

28
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:53,220
Damn it.

29
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:57,660
These guys have been lucky since summer

30
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:02,080
Lost property, is it?

31
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:03,420
Thanks for your trouble.

32
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,480
Good work.

33
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:06,360
You don't need it, do you?

34
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:08,740
Lost items should be
turned in to the police.

35
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:11,340
That's common sense in Japan, right?

36
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:15,080
Yes, come to the police box later and
I'll give you ten percent as a reward.

37
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:16,920
I'll give you at least one noodle.

38
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:22,080
Don't need that stuff.

39
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:24,840
That was close, surviving until payday.

40
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:28,220
Even one cup noodle is precious food,
after all.

41
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:31,760
That one's a miss too

42
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:32,740
So close.

43
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:34,700
What are you doing?

44
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:38,060
I'm checking the lottery results.

45
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:40,200
Four of us bought forty tickets.

46
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:44,780
Pulling this nonsense while on duty!

47
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:47,500
Once in a while,
discuss world affairs or something.

48
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:50,120
Peace talks about
Bosnia-Herzegovina or whatever.

49
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,860
Bosnia-Herzegovina?

50
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:53,940
Chief, don't you know?

51
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:55,960
Yugoslavia broke apart, you see.

52
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:59,200
If you're going to say that,
it's Bosnia-Herzegovina.

53
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,220
You, who's always absorbed in gambling,

54
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:04,840
have no right to criticize me.

55
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:09,380
The lottery isn't gambling.

56
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:17,440
That's what gambling is.

57
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:19,540
Oddly convincing, isn't it.

58
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:23,100
Thinking you'll hit it big
with a book like that is naive.

59
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:26,240
If you want to make money,
pour in your time and money.

60
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:28,520
Let's leave him be and look into it.

61
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,240
Yes, that's right.

62
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:31,580
Four left.

63
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:34,400
This one's wrong.

64
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,040
Your thinking is wrong.

65
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:38,500
Work to live up to expectations.

66
00:03:42,620 --> 00:03:43,560
So they're all losers?

67
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:45,360
Of course they are.

68
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:48,040
That Bajiadarma you two read,

69
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:50,180
the goddess of luck never smiled on it.

70
00:03:52,060 --> 00:03:52,340
Right.

71
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:55,880
Maybe last year's same lottery
tickets are still left over.

72
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:56,920
Let's look into it.

73
00:03:57,480 --> 00:04:00,340
This book should list the
winning numbers for the whole year.

74
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:01,360
Yeah, that's right.

75
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:03,880
There's one left.

76
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:06,380
You know, the reason I hate lotteries is

77
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:08,300
because the winners hide their tickets.

78
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:13,840
First prize's no good,
second prize's no good, third prize too?

79
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:20,060
I won 3 million yen!

80
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:27,240
Come to think of it, in Japan they don't announce winners
proudly in front of the media like they do overseas, do they?

81
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:29,680
That's the bad side of
stingy Japanese people.

82
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:31,180
Hey, Chief.

83
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:35,120
Keeping quiet when you've
won isn't right, is it?

84
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:35,260
Hey.

85
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:37,900
Y-yeah, you're right.

86
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:40,780
Compared to that, people who play
pachinko or the horses are better.

87
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:44,060
Whether they win or lose,
their feelings show honestly.

88
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:46,860
Ryo-chan,
you lost at pachinko today, didn't you?

89
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:50,480
Shut up, winning and losing
is just the luck of the draw.

90
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:51,700
Chief.

91
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:54,400
How did the lottery go?

92
00:04:56,780 --> 00:04:58,600
That? Lost.

93
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,760
Enough about the lottery.

94
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:03,360
Let's talk about Herzegovina with the boss,
shall we?

95
00:05:06,620 --> 00:05:12,540
You're not hiding something, are you?
Not at all. Is that so?

96
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:21,520
Lottery winners have a pattern: the moment they win,
they suddenly go quiet and

97
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:22,120
become distant.

98
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:28,200
Before long, they change the subject
and stop talking about the lottery.

99
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,700
Show me that lottery ticket.

100
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:35,160
It's a loser, it's a loser!

101
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:36,740
If it's a loser, can I take a look?

102
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:37,840
No way, no way!

103
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:40,360
Let me slip up.

104
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:44,960
If I get worked up,
I'll look even more suspicious.

105
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:46,220
I'm not getting worked up!

106
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:48,660
It's a loser, so I'm saying it's a loser!

107
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:50,740
He's saying it himself,
so there's no mistake.

108
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:52,100
You're really getting worked up, aren't you.

109
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,140
Oh, no...

110
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:57,180
Then tear that ticket up right here.

111
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:58,260
What?

112
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:02,540
It's a loser, isn't it?
Or should I tear it up for you?

113
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:06,440
N-no, I'm collecting losing tickets.

114
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:07,560
Heh heh heh.

115
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:09,740
When did you start
doing something like that?

116
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:12,380
Your eyes are lying!

117
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:13,340
Show me!

118
00:06:13,420 --> 00:06:16,780
What are you doing?
Hey, s-stop, stop! It's going to tear!

119
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:17,820
Why does it stink?

120
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:18,980
Knock it off!

121
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:23,040
Ryo-chan, are you okay?

122
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:23,980
Senpai!

123
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:28,740
That move won't win you
100,000 or 200,000 yen.

124
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:30,760
I figured it was a considerable amount.

125
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:33,480
Check it against that book.

126
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:34,260
Yes.

127
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:37,020
Which lottery ticket did the Chief buy?

128
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:40,020
It's the same as this year's.

129
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:43,360
This one.

130
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:44,220
Okay.

131
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:47,100
I'll read out the prize
amounts from the bottom.

132
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:47,800
Yes.

133
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,400
Fifth prize, 500,000 yen.

134
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:53,560
Wrong.

135
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:56,720
Fourth prize, 1,000,000 yen.

136
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:01,200
This one's not it either.

137
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:01,820
Next.

138
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:03,540
3rd prize, three million.

139
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:09,540
Got it.

140
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,600
It's a three-million-yen winner!

141
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:13,140
No, wait.

142
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:18,060
Petty little people like the Chief
get jittery and it shows on their faces.

143
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:19,540
It's definitely three million yen.

144
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:22,400
Wrong! It's a loser!

145
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:26,500
Banks check winnings over one million yen very strictly,
you know.

146
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,480
That lottery ticket expires today.

147
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:33,660
If you don't claim it today,
it becomes void.

148
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:44,540
That's all for today. Let's go drinking.

149
00:07:44,540 --> 00:07:46,200
Until midnight.

150
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:51,700
Sorry, I actually won 3 million yen.

151
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:53,220
Chief, you did it!

152
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:57,380
But you didn't do anything wrong,
so there's no need to hide it.

153
00:07:57,380 --> 00:07:59,140
Well, yes, but...

154
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:02,900
It's the bad Japanese habit of never
showing what you feel on your face.

155
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:07,480
You should express your joy with your whole body,
like foreigners do.

156
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:08,700
Like this!

157
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:12,080
Yay! I won the lottery!

158
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:13,560
Shut up!

159
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:17,160
Yeah! Gundam! Give me the spread!

160
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:20,936
Well,

161
00:08:20,986 --> 00:08:24,680
I'd like you to express
your joy at about this level.

162
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:25,960
Understood?

163
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,500
There's no such foreigner.

164
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:30,900
Let's call the station right
away and let everyone know.

165
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:33,140
Hey, you!

166
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:36,520
You only found out you won because you happened to check,
didn't you?

167
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:39,200
It's just like a hole-in-one in golf.

168
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:42,620
Throwing a party and celebrating
together is just common sense.

169
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:48,460
Or were you planning to hog the
3 million yen all to yourself?

170
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:51,280
I had no such intention at all.

171
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:53,740
In that case, leave it to me.

172
00:08:55,460 --> 00:09:02,380
Ryotsu of Kameari Park-mae is hosting a banquet for 200 people tonight,
so prepare the finest shabu-shabu.

173
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,820
Shabu-shabu.

174
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:06,720
Hey.

175
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:11,160
Well then,
I'll go let the station know in person.

176
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:12,520
Ryotsu.

177
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:15,680
Winning the lottery was lucky, but

178
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:18,820
it was unlucky that Ryo-chan was here.

179
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:31,000
Chief's taking another day off today

180
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:34,040
He's been out ever since
the day after that incident.

181
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:36,640
It's about time he pulled himself together,

182
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:38,600
but he really took it hard.

183
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:40,800
Ryo-san went a bit too far, though.

184
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:43,000
He should've stopped at the shabu-shabu.

185
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:45,240
They booked the place for eight hours,
after all.

186
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:47,260
The Chief just came in to work.

187
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:53,680
Good morning.

188
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:56,180
I'm sorry for causing you all trouble.

189
00:09:57,220 --> 00:10:00,500
How much did that party end up costing?

190
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:03,260
Not a single sen was left.

191
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:06,300
Sorry, but please don't bring that up again.

192
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,520
It just makes my fever flare up again.

193
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:13,860
Anyway, Chief, ever since that,
I've become totally hooked on lotteries.

194
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:14,320
What?

195
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:16,680
It's an American lotto, you know.

196
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:17,720
What's that supposed to be?

197
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:23,060
You pick six numbers from 1 to 51,
and if they all match, you win.

198
00:10:23,060 --> 00:10:26,200
Apparently, the jackpot is 5.5 billion yen.

199
00:10:27,420 --> 00:10:29,020
5.5 billion yen?

200
00:10:33,340 --> 00:10:35,840
I can see why the four of them are hooked,

201
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:39,300
but there's no way it wins that easily.

202
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:42,460
That's why he says there
might be a Ryo-chan Law.

203
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:44,560
He's been collecting
five years' worth of data,

204
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:46,400
and going to see a mathematician,

205
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:48,880
to study which number combinations will hit.

206
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:51,720
He's diligent about everything except work.

207
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:55,300
Chief, you've finally come out?

208
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:58,740
Ryotsu, you mocked lotteries so much,

209
00:10:58,740 --> 00:11:00,900
yet I hear you've been
buying them up by the dozen.

210
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:02,760
Come on, don't be so stiff about it.

211
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:05,340
I mean,
we're talking about 5.5 billion yen here.

212
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:08,080
Ryo-san, a notice came from overseas.

213
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:11,480
Alright, alright, I'll keep buying until I win,
even if it takes my whole life.

214
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:15,580
Chief, why don't you buy a share
in the 5.5 billion yen dream too?

215
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:17,980
No, I'm good.

216
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:19,136
Well,

217
00:11:19,186 --> 00:11:22,760
you should just chase your modest little dreams in Japan,
steady and simple.

218
00:11:23,300 --> 00:11:25,140
Well then, let's see if it's a winner.

219
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:27,720
Let's see,
the winning numbers from last time were,

220
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,920
2, 16, 17?

221
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:34,140
So far, they match!

222
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:36,240
23?

223
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:37,120
2?

224
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:37,880
34?

225
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:39,540
It matches!

226
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:43,353
No, you got me all excited up to here,

227
00:11:43,403 --> 00:11:45,660
and now you're going to let me down,
aren't you?

228
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,580
See, I knew it.

229
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:50,600
But the numbers I picked were 45...

230
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:52,400
Damn it, why didn't I just go with 45?

231
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:53,560
On a measly 45...

232
00:11:55,260 --> 00:11:57,040
45... could it be that...

233
00:11:57,900 --> 00:11:59,200
Could it be...

234
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:01,540
45

235
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:10,620
It's a match!

236
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,600
5.5 billion yen

237
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:14,960
It's a match!

238
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:43,580
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

239
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:44,100
That was a bad thing to say.

240
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:48,260
Hey, was he sleepwalking? W-wait, a fever...

241
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:50,220
Anyway, how did the lotto go?

242
00:12:50,780 --> 00:12:52,420
What are you talking about?

243
00:12:53,100 --> 00:12:56,080
You were just checking the American Lotto winning numbers,
weren't you?

244
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,260
You scared me!

245
00:12:58,260 --> 00:13:01,800
Anyway, why don't we all talk
about revising the consumption tax?

246
00:13:02,380 --> 00:13:03,300
Right?

247
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:08,307
Let's see, the behavior patterns of winners,
if I recall correctly,

248
00:13:08,357 --> 00:13:11,540
they change the subject and
stop talking about lotteries.

249
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:15,520
What happened with the lotto, Ryotsu?

250
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:18,500
Anyway, let's set that aside.

251
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:22,540
I'm on duty,
so please don't talk to me for a while.

252
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:26,420
Then they suddenly go
quiet and turn distant.

253
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:28,800
Come on.

254
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:32,060
I'm naturally quiet, you know.

255
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:39,800
You hit it, didn't you?

256
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:42,720
What are you talking about?

257
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:45,120
Wakuwaku...

258
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:47,540
Don't play dumb. You won, didn't you?

259
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:49,060
Won what~?

260
00:13:49,060 --> 00:13:51,440
The numbers hit, didn't they?

261
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:53,220
5.5 billion

262
00:13:53,220 --> 00:13:55,600
You won 5.5 billion yen, didn't you?

263
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:57,800
Uwaaah... me...

264
00:13:57,800 --> 00:13:58,560
Nothing at all.

265
00:13:58,560 --> 00:14:01,320
It matches. The numbers you picked, senior,

266
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:02,400
are the same as mine.

267
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:04,240
Hey, Nakagawa!

268
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:06,300
You copied my picks, didn't you!

269
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:07,600
That's dirty, you bastard!

270
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:11,220
But we were picking the numbers together!

271
00:14:11,540 --> 00:14:12,980
Stop it, Ryo-chan!

272
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:14,540
So it really hit?

273
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:17,580
5.5 billion yen, for real.

274
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:20,380
It hit, didn't it!

275
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:25,060
Yes.

276
00:14:26,020 --> 00:14:29,960
What? You're the one who told
everyone to go wild like foreigners!

277
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:33,040
Look who's talking,
the poster boy for the little guy.

278
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:36,040
Don't get the wrong idea.

279
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:38,860
We're about to go wild like foreigners,
you know.

280
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:40,540
Here goes.

281
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,400
Happy Stay

282
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:45,260
I won 5.5 billion yen!

283
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:46,560
Ooh, so close!

284
00:14:46,980 --> 00:14:49,000
Buzz!

285
00:14:49,530 --> 00:14:51,040
Give me chocolate!

286
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:53,040
Making us wait for 5.5 billion yen...

287
00:14:53,040 --> 00:14:54,100
What beautiful weather.

288
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:55,920
No, look!

289
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:58,200
He's completely tripping over his own feet.

290
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,580
Happy day!

291
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:01,160
I won 5.5 billion yen!

292
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:12,040
It's rare to see someone hide
their agitation this badly.

293
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:14,100
You should just be happy
like a normal person.

294
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:16,860
Since it's a special occasion,
let's notify the press.

295
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:19,360
Wait, please.

296
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:26,960
You said that at times like this we should tell everyone and celebrate,
didn't you, Ryotsu?

297
00:15:28,520 --> 00:15:29,720
That's right.

298
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:34,200
I wish you'd let everyone in Japan know!

299
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:37,620
Hello, this is Kameari Park police box.

300
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:40,860
At this rate,
things are going to get crazy from tomorrow.

301
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:41,820
Yes.

302
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:53,800
Senpai, you've become a celebrity overnight.

303
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:57,640
Damn it, every one of them thinks they can say whatever they want,
just because it's a single line.

304
00:15:57,640 --> 00:16:00,120
Look, Kou,
so many letters have come for you.

305
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:00,680
What?

306
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:04,460
From Mr. M.K.,
who lives in Chiba Prefecture.

307
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:07,780
Hogging 5.5 billion yen all to yourself,
you bastard.

308
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:10,220
You're not going to use it properly anyway,
are you?

309
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:12,520
Go straight to the bottom of hell,
you son of a bitch.

310
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:13,760
But...

311
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:14,360
Don't mess with me!

312
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:21,380
Move, move, move!

313
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:26,800
K-Komachi and Naoko!

314
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:28,960
Ryo-sama, marry me!

315
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:32,080
I've admired you for ages, Ryo-sama!

316
00:16:32,620 --> 00:16:33,720
Ryo-sama?

317
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:39,980
I always knew you'd do something big,
Ryo-sama!

318
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:43,420
Hey, I'd have a wedding
with Ryo-sama right away!

319
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:45,260
Hey, wait, Komachi!

320
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:46,940
Fine by me, Naoko!

321
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:50,100
I'm the one who's going to marry Ryo-sama!

322
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:51,840
Ryo-chan, until yesterday,

323
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:55,000
you were the number one man in
the precinct nobody wanted to marry.

324
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,515
Shut up! Before I'd marry either of you,

325
00:16:57,565 --> 00:16:59,980
I'd throw 5.5 billion yen down the drain!

326
00:17:00,260 --> 00:17:03,080
What did you say? How rude!

327
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:05,160
BEEP!

328
00:17:05,760 --> 00:17:07,720
Hey! Ryotsu! Do something about this!

329
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:08,560
Chief!

330
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:12,080
This panic won't die down
unless you go out there!

331
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:13,980
Every last one of you!

332
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:14,980
There you go!

333
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:16,580
Hurry up and get out of here!

334
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:20,440
Now the sister of the person in charge's
father's brother is showing up too!

335
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:24,520
I haven't gotten the 5.5 billion yen yet,
so it's all no comment!

336
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:25,780
But, well...

337
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:26,720
Don't make excuses.

338
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:32,660
Once the cash arrives,
I'll answer anything you want,

339
00:17:32,660 --> 00:17:33,980
and I'll announce how I'm going to spend it.

340
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:36,360
So everyone, go home today.

341
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:39,480
Well then, bye-bye, goodbye!

342
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:45,280
What?

343
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:48,140
Got it.

344
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:50,360
What happened?

345
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:52,860
They said the money came in from America.

346
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:53,020
So?

347
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:55,200
The transfer is 5.5 billion.

348
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:55,860
Shh!

349
00:17:57,020 --> 00:17:58,040
Keep your voice down.

350
00:17:58,040 --> 00:18:00,100
The press will come rushing over, you know!

351
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:01,800
You're not going to tell the press?

352
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:02,600
Of course not.

353
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:03,780
Anyway, I'm going to go pick it up.

354
00:18:03,780 --> 00:18:04,740
Leave the rest to you.

355
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:18,400
We've arrived.

356
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:20,040
Here you are, master.

357
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:22,160
Good work.

358
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:45,800
It's not a
"Master" blend, it's a brand name.

359
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:48,620
Sanzaiyu

360
00:18:49,460 --> 00:18:50,880
I'm terribly sorry.

361
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:52,040
Let me introduce him.

362
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:55,600
This is Sato,
who will be working as my butler from today.

363
00:18:56,940 --> 00:18:57,900
I'm Sato.

364
00:18:57,900 --> 00:19:00,520
I look forward to working with you.

365
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:02,140
Hi, I'm Nakagawa.

366
00:19:02,140 --> 00:19:02,980
I'm Reiko.

367
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:04,700
I'm Chief Ohara.

368
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:09,340
Nakagawa and Reiko,
I'm always indebted to you two.

369
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:11,560
I'll go tell them.

370
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:13,180
W-this much?

371
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:14,560
Can I really take it?

372
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,360
Of course.

373
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:17,540
R-Ryotsu...

374
00:19:17,540 --> 00:19:19,460
Don't spend it so freely!

375
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:20,960
Save it! Put it in savings!

376
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:22,320
Sandayu!

377
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:24,560
Bring the thing to the Chief.

378
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:26,820
W-what is it?

379
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:30,640
After all, we made you spend three
million yen at the banquet the other day.

380
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:32,440
Please take this as an apology.

381
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:37,960
T-t-this much!

382
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:39,340
Is it all right?

383
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:40,180
Here you go.

384
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:42,240
Let's do that thing.

385
00:19:42,780 --> 00:19:45,580
Sandayu, about 300 million yen more,
to the room...

386
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:46,900
Very well, sir.

387
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:53,440
Doing something like this...

388
00:19:59,380 --> 00:20:01,840
I've always wanted to
try this once I got rich.

389
00:20:04,320 --> 00:20:05,880
I can't wait for the fancy dinner!

390
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:07,920
Chief, please don't hold back.

391
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:10,580
You fool!
Do you think I'd do something like that?

392
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:11,820
I'm no money-grubber!

393
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:15,100
You should make the most of
seeing cash while you still can.

394
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:16,380
While we still can?

395
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:19,640
Ryotsu, have you already
decided what to spend it on?

396
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:22,576
Hey, you placed an order the day you won,

397
00:20:22,626 --> 00:20:24,000
and I thought it would arrive today.

398
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,940
Looks like it's arrived.

399
00:20:26,940 --> 00:20:29,240
What did he order?

400
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:37,760
That guy bought a real combat helicopter

401
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:39,780
and paid for it in gold

402
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:43,440
Idiot, a real one would
cost over 10 billion yen!

403
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:48,300
I was surprised,
but of course I can't buy a real one.

404
00:20:48,300 --> 00:20:51,420
This is a full-scale
radio-controlled helicopter.

405
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:55,040
It looks just like the real thing,
and it's a custom order with gold plating.

406
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:56,780
All told, 5 billion yen.

407
00:20:57,580 --> 00:20:58,840
My head hurts...

408
00:20:59,240 --> 00:20:59,780
Chief!

409
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:01,640
Did you load that up?

410
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:02,960
Yes, it's already done.

411
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,180
Right, let's do the first flight right away!

412
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:09,840
Welcome again, drive-thru customers!

413
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:17,440
Yes!

414
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:23,340
Flew to the heliport!

415
00:21:23,340 --> 00:21:25,520
Senpai, what's he planning to do?

416
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:29,260
This is amazing,
it's like flying a real helicopter.

417
00:21:29,260 --> 00:21:35,340
If I'm spending 5.5 billion yen anyway, this
suits me far better than saving or donating.

418
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:38,860
Alright, let's scatter it all over the park.

419
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:46,520
Aaaaah!

420
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:48,320
Aaaaah!

421
00:21:50,540 --> 00:21:52,480
Gimme, gimme, you common folk!

422
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:55,660
I gave 5.5 billion yen at Sensō-ji.

423
00:21:55,660 --> 00:21:57,000
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu!

424
00:21:58,160 --> 00:22:01,040
Hogging this luck all to myself

425
00:22:01,040 --> 00:22:01,760
would be greedy.

426
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:04,440
I'll share some with you all

427
00:22:05,640 --> 00:22:06,880
Accept this gift!

428
00:22:08,780 --> 00:22:10,840
A lottery win What a sudden thing.

429
00:22:10,840 --> 00:22:12,980
But he's really scattering it around in style,
isn't he?

430
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:15,680
It's six hundred million yen's worth,
after all.

431
00:22:15,680 --> 00:22:17,600
Five hundred million yen's worth?

432
00:22:19,360 --> 00:22:20,400
Pick it up, pick it up!

433
00:22:27,820 --> 00:22:30,160
Take this along with it while you're at it.

434
00:22:32,120 --> 00:22:33,400
This is so much fun!

435
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:36,060
Take this one too while you're at it.

436
00:22:36,060 --> 00:22:38,260
And while you're at that,

437
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:39,300
take this one too.

438
00:22:45,080 --> 00:22:46,160
Oh no.

439
00:22:47,860 --> 00:22:49,380
The transmitter...

440
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:52,100
Without the transmitter,

441
00:22:52,660 --> 00:22:53,820
I can't control it.

442
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:04,460
What do we do?

443
00:23:04,460 --> 00:23:05,180
Super...

444
00:23:07,740 --> 00:23:10,120
My helicopter...

445
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:13,280
My 5 billion yen helicopter...

446
00:23:14,760 --> 00:23:16,380
My pay...

447
00:23:16,380 --> 00:23:18,460
Ryo-san, this is bad!

448
00:23:18,460 --> 00:23:22,940
Apparently the lottery prize is
subject to a 30% US federal tax.

449
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:28,260
They say you have to pay 30%
of the 5.5 billion yen in taxes.

450
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,220
30% of 5.5 billion yen?

451
00:23:33,780 --> 00:23:35,600
1.65 billion yen?

452
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:36,400
Clink

453
00:23:42,660 --> 00:23:47,140
You made 5.5 billion yen and
blew through it in no time.

454
00:23:47,140 --> 00:23:52,400
And on top of that, you've gone and
racked up 1.65 billion yen in debt.

455
00:23:52,960 --> 00:23:54,980
What a textbook example of an idiot.

456
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:07,220
Step right up, step right up, come and see!

457
00:24:07,220 --> 00:24:09,640
Snow falling in midsummer at Kameyari!

458
00:24:10,160 --> 00:24:11,500
On hot days, shaved ice.

459
00:24:11,500 --> 00:24:13,900
Mass-produced special,
imported straight from Alaska.

460
00:24:13,900 --> 00:24:16,060
Won't you buy a giant shaved ice?

461
00:24:16,720 --> 00:24:19,340
Next time, shaved ice, to each their own.

462
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:20,760
Take care.

463
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:36,680
Let's always smile, okay?

464
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:40,900
no matter how outrageous things get,

465
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:45,380
keep smiling sweetly, okay?

466
00:24:45,380 --> 00:24:50,600
just head out with a carefree face.

467
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:54,080
Hey, smile for me, won't you?

468
00:24:54,080 --> 00:24:57,440
It's not your fault.

469
00:24:58,840 --> 00:25:02,820
Hey, smile for me, won't you?

470
00:25:02,820 --> 00:25:05,760
Keep up the same mood as before.

471
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:11,580
Keep smiling all the time, okay?

472
00:25:11,580 --> 00:25:16,540
Women who act all serious aren't pretty,

473
00:25:16,540 --> 00:25:21,380
so you should smile right away.

474
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:25,840
Unless you're a child, that is.

475
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,800
Thanks for watching.

